      "id": "z7mhkm0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. What is Humidity?"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Humidity represents the quantity of water vapour present in the atmosphere and varies directly with air temperature.",
        "Saturation occurs when air holds the maximum possible amount of water vapour at a given temperature, resulting in 100% Relative Humidity.",
        "Dew Point is the critical temperature at which air becomes completely saturated and condensation begins.",
        "Clouds form when ascending air cools to its dew point, condensing around microscopic condensation nuclei.",
        "Precipitation is the final stage of the atmospheric moisture cycle, occurring as rain, snow, hail, or sleet."
      ],
      "id": "4qu0xpu"
    },
