    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Relative Humidity shares an inverse relationship with temperature: as air temperature rises without added moisture, Relative Humidity decreases.",
        "Orographic rainfall creates a moist windward side and a dry leeward side known as a rain-shadow region.",
        "When dry bulb and wet bulb thermometer readings on a psychrometer are identical, Relative Humidity is 100%."
      ],
